Task A1: Design the Data Acquisition  [7 Marks | K3 – Apply]
A1.1: Inspect the Source (2 Marks)
Each of the 12 monitoring stations transmits a daily comma-separated values (CSV) file containing 24 hourly rows (288 total readings per day across the network). Each file contains 7 expected columns: station, date, hour, pm25, pm10, no2, and temp.
Data-Quality Defect	Description & Root Cause	Concrete Raw Example
Missing Values	Sensor dropout or network packet loss recorded as blank string or 'NA'.	Adyar,2026-10-01,09:00,NA,85.0,26.1,32.0
Negative Readings	Zero-point calibration drift producing physically impossible negative concentrations.	Guindy,2026-10-01,09:00,-12.5,140.0,42.3,89.6
