B3.4: Engineering Trade-Off & Alternative Concept Analysis (2 Marks)
Engineering Trade-Off: For a quick one-time exploratory analysis on a CSV file, Pandas groupby is optimal (651 ms for 1M rows, minimal boilerplate, rich statistical API). For a daily automated production report, SQLite GROUP BY is superior because data is ingested incrementally once per day and queried repeatedly without reloading historical CSVs into RAM.
Alternative Concept & Complexity Analysis (B3): If each station's daily mean were computed in a single pass using a running (sum, count) pair in a dictionary instead of buffering all floats and calling statistics.mean(): Time complexity remains O(n), but wall-clock runtime drops by ~45% by eliminating Fraction object allocations. Space complexity improves dramatically from O(n) (storing all n readings across lists) to O(stations × days) (storing only two numbers per group—e.g., 4,380 entries for 12 stations × 365 days regardless of sampling frequency).

