Alternative Concept & Complexity Analysis (B4): If the extractive summariser picked the first k sentences of each complaint (Lead-k baseline) instead of scoring sentences by important word frequencies: Lead-k runs in O(1) time and O(1) space per document (versus O(W) time and O(V) vocabulary space for frequency scoring). However, on citizen complaints, citizens frequently open with greetings or administrative preamble ('Respected Sir, I am a resident of Ward 14...') before stating the core hazard ('...thick black smoke is emitted every midnight'). Frequency-based extraction captures the high-signal hazard sentences, whereas Lead-k truncates them.
